---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Your data · IDC Revision">
  <article class="progress-page privacy reading">
    <h1 class="page-title">Your data</h1>
    <p class="privacy-lede">A plain-language note on what this site keeps, where, and what you can do about it.</p>

    <h2>Without an account</h2>
    <p>
      Everything you tick, the lectures you mark as read and your semester stay in your browser on this device.
      None of it is sent anywhere. Clearing your browser's site data removes it.
    </p>

    <h2>With an account</h2>
    <p>Signing in saves the following to your account, so it follows you between devices:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>your email address and name, from your sign-in;</li>
      <li>each tick and lecture read, with when you made it (including a history of changes);</li>
      <li>the days you revised, the badges you earned and the last page you opened in each course.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Sign-in is handled by <a href="https://clerk.com" rel="noopener">Clerk</a>, which sets the cookies needed to keep
      you signed in (<a href="https://clerk.com/legal/privacy" rel="noopener">Clerk's privacy policy</a>). Your progress
      is stored in a Postgres database hosted by <a href="https://neon.com" rel="noopener">Neon</a> in Frankfurt.
    </p>

    <h2>Who can see it</h2>
    <p>
      Only you. The site's maintainer sees course-wide totals, such as how many students got a question wrong,
      and only for groups of five or more students, so no one's individual activity can be picked out.
      Page visits are counted with Vercel's cookie-free analytics.
    </p>

    <h2>What you can do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Download your data</strong> from the You page, as one file.</li>
      <li><strong>Sign out</strong> to remove your progress from a device. It stays in your account.</li>
      <li><strong>Delete your account</strong> from the You page. Your account and all its progress are removed straight away.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Layout>
